openmediavault-frpc (8.0.4) stable; urgency=medium

  * Make the generated frpc.toml valid for the bundled frpc 0.71.0:
    - Remove the "Print proxied content" option; it wrote an unsupported
      "printContent" key into [log], so frpc refused to start with
      'json: unknown field "printContent"'.
    - Write the client metadata to [metadatas] instead of the
      unsupported [meta] table.
    - Write transport multiplexing as tcpMux = true instead of the
      unsupported [transport.multiplexer] table.
    - Emit type specific proxy keys only for the proxy types frpc
      accepts them for: secretKey for stcp/xtcp/sudp; subdomain and
      customDomains for http/https/tcpmux; locations, hostHeaderRewrite,
      httpUser and httpPassword for http only.
    - Skip empty entries when rendering "includes" and "meta". OMV
      stores empty array properties as empty XML elements, which were
      rendered as includes = [""].
  * The proxy form shows subdomain and custom domains for tcpmux (frp
    requires at least one of them) and host header rewrite for http only.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER}  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-frpc (8.0.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Salt state fix: the native backend branch declared the state ID
    "frpc_systemctl_daemon_reload" twice when the service was disabled,
    so "Apply" failed with "found conflicting ID". The systemd unit is
    now created only while the service is enabled, and stopping the
    service is skipped when no unit file exists.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER}  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:45:00 +0800

openmediavault-frpc (8.0.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix configuration read/write failure ("Failed to index key 'user' of
    'user.0'") caused by data model property names that collide with the
    OMV reserved configuration key list ($enums). Rename the settings
    "user" property to "userPrefix" and the proxy "group" property to
    "loadBalancerGroup". Form labels, translations and the generated
    frpc.toml keys (user, loadBalancer.group) are unchanged.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER}  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0800

openmediavault-frpc (8.0.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: FRP client (frpc) management plugin for
    OpenMediaVault 8.x, modeled after the OpenWrt luci-app-frpc
    plugins.
    - Settings: frps server, token, transport (tcp/kcp/quic/ws/wss),
      TLS, multiplexing, connection pool, heartbeat, proxy URL, DNS,
      logging and the frpc admin web server.
    - Proxies/visitors: tcp, udp, http, https, tcpmux, stcp, xtcp
      and sudp with local/remote ports, secret keys, visitor binding,
      domains and subdomains, basic HTTP auth, encryption,
      compression, bandwidth limit, PROXY protocol, load-balancer
      groups, health checks and a raw TOML escape hatch.
    - Two selectable backends: an existing Docker frpc container
      (default) or the bundled frpc binary with a generated systemd
      unit (native).
    - Start/stop/restart buttons, frpc hot reload, live per-proxy
      status through the admin API, log viewer and generated
      frpc.toml preview.
    - Simplified and Traditional Chinese translations included.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER}  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0800
